@pgxsinkit/pgwasm-c
===================

This package republishes compiled third-party software and includes host code that
began as a copy of third-party code. These attributions are permanent.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ElectricSQL — @electric-sql/pglite (host code under `src/`)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The C build's host code under `src/` (module instantiation, initdb, the memory,
IndexedDB and file mounts, the filesystem adapter, extension install) began as a copy
of ElectricSQL's PGlite (`packages/pglite`, `packages/pglite-utils`):

  Source:  https://github.com/electric-sql/pglite
  License: PostgreSQL License (PGlite is dual-licensed Apache-2.0 / PostgreSQL
           License; pgxsinkit takes it under the PostgreSQL License)
  Copyright (c) ElectricSQL and contributors

Owned outright (ADR-0062); compatibility with PGlite is an explicit anti-goal. The
PostgreSQL License text is in LICENSE.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The artefacts, and what is compiled into them
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`artefacts/` holds six files republished byte-identical from `@electric-sql/pglite`
0.5.8 (https://registry.npmjs.org/@electric-sql/pglite/-/pglite-0.5.8.tgz; the
tarball's integrity and every file's sha256 are pinned in `src/artefact-pins.ts`):
`pglite.wasm` (the Postgres server), `pglite.data` (its filesystem bundle: share
files, loadable modules, time zone data, ICU data), `pglite.js` and `initdb.js`
(Emscripten-generated JavaScript), `initdb.wasm` (initdb) and `amcheck.tar.gz` (the
amcheck extension).

They were built by ElectricSQL from the postgres-pglite tree
(https://github.com/electric-sql/postgres-pglite, commit b133782cd759f08b3aeb263b80a963b39c7b7af1,
the commit the @electric-sql/pglite@0.5.8 release tag of github.com/electric-sql/pglite
pins) inside the builder image
`electricsql/pglite-builder:3.1.74-7`, whose recipe is that tree's
`pglite/builder/Dockerfile`. The components below, and their versions, come from:

  - the configure line embedded in pglite.wasm: --with-icu --with-uuid=ossp
    --with-zlib --with-libxml --with-libxslt --with-openssl=no --without-llvm, and
    its server link line (-lxslt -lxml2 -lz, and ICU through ICU_LIBS);
  - the builder Dockerfile: Emscripten 3.1.74, zlib 1.3.1, libxml2 2.14.5,
    libxslt 1.1.43, ICU 76.1. The binaries confirm Emscripten 3.1.74 (in the
    server's version string) and ICU 76 (its data package, icudt76l);
  - the files of pglite.data (dict_snowball.so, the time zone data, the ICU data and
    its LICENSE).

Not included: OpenSSL (--with-openssl=no), LLVM (--without-llvm), and OSSP uuid —
configure enables it, but only the uuid-ossp extension links it, and that extension
is not part of these artefacts. The builder image's other libraries (for PostGIS and
pgcrypto) belong to extensions that are not shipped either.

Each component's notice follows, copied from the file named with it.

